1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,000
 Okay, there are two approaches in performing a replacement study.

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:15,359
 First one is when no study period is specified, the second one is when a study period is specified.

3
00:00:15,359 --> 00:00:18,240
 Let's take them one by one.

4
00:00:18,240 --> 00:00:25,500
 So no study period specified, you see, well it's the left branch of our tree that we also

5
00:00:25,500 --> 00:00:27,280
 had on the previous slide.

6
00:00:27,280 --> 00:00:30,820
 And here you see the procedure.

7
00:00:30,820 --> 00:00:37,240
 So basically we start with calculating the annual worth.

8
00:00:37,240 --> 00:00:44,520
 We look when the economic service life is reached and we select the lower annual worth.

9
00:00:44,520 --> 00:00:47,880
 If that was the challenger, it's easy.

10
00:00:47,880 --> 00:00:52,920
 We just replace the defender by the challenger.

11
00:00:52,920 --> 00:01:03,000
 If the defender is selected, we will keep him for one year and then repeat the analysis.

12
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:04,000
 Why is that?

13
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:06,480
 Well it has to do with estimates.

14
00:01:06,480 --> 00:01:11,640
 We're working with estimates and usually our estimates are not so accurate if we go further

15
00:01:11,640 --> 00:01:12,799
 and further in the future.

16
00:01:12,799 --> 00:01:21,640
 So we will repeat that analysis every year.

17
00:01:21,719 --> 00:01:25,239
 Okay, now an example.

18
00:01:25,239 --> 00:01:26,239
 So we have an example.

19
00:01:26,239 --> 00:01:28,040
 It's a rather long story.

20
00:01:28,040 --> 00:01:32,280
 There's a lot of information which is nice to know but not need to know.

21
00:01:32,280 --> 00:01:37,079
 So basically it's about a company Toshiba Electronics that invested in a new assembly

22
00:01:37,079 --> 00:01:44,680
 line two years ago and they purchased approximately 200 units at 70,000 each and installed them

23
00:01:44,680 --> 00:01:49,560
 in different countries and then we get quite some explanation about what the equipment

24
00:01:49,560 --> 00:01:51,040
 is about.

25
00:01:51,040 --> 00:01:57,440
 Now this year, that's important for our study, new industrial standards will require 60,000

26
00:01:57,440 --> 00:01:59,880
 retrofit for each of the units.

27
00:01:59,880 --> 00:02:04,280
 That's an extra cost so it's not included in the expected operating costs that they

28
00:02:04,280 --> 00:02:05,960
 had so far.

29
00:02:05,960 --> 00:02:08,740
 Also a new system is available.

30
00:02:08,740 --> 00:02:12,259
 It can be considered as a challenger to the old system.

31
00:02:12,259 --> 00:02:16,659
 Now the data you find there.

32
00:02:16,659 --> 00:02:19,899
 Now for challenger and defender.

33
00:02:19,899 --> 00:02:24,099
 And the chief engineer asks for a replacement study to be performed this year and each year

34
00:02:24,099 --> 00:02:26,539
 in the future if needed.

35
00:02:26,539 --> 00:02:30,340
 Interest rate considered is 10%.

36
00:02:30,340 --> 00:02:37,060
 So step that we want to take is first we need to compute economic service life.

37
00:02:37,060 --> 00:02:44,300
 We have to see whether we keep the defender or we will go for a challenger and then we

38
00:02:44,300 --> 00:02:49,099
 will do a follow-up analysis after one year and also there we have the data which are

39
00:02:49,099 --> 00:02:54,060
 outlined in C.

40
00:02:54,060 --> 00:02:58,099
 So this is the data summarized.

41
00:02:58,099 --> 00:03:05,860
 For the first part you see, well I wrote them out for you to the left and you see the table

42
00:03:06,340 --> 00:03:07,340
 to the right.

43
00:03:07,340 --> 00:03:13,940
 What you see also in the right table is that they already computed the total annual worth

44
00:03:13,940 --> 00:03:21,180
 and expected, sorry, I'm making the mistake myself, the economic service life here is

45
00:03:21,180 --> 00:03:24,980
 four years, here it's three years.

46
00:03:24,980 --> 00:03:27,660
 How do we compute this total annual worth?

47
00:03:27,660 --> 00:03:31,980
 Well exactly the same way as was done before.

48
00:03:32,019 --> 00:03:40,500
 In the examples, well for your convenience I included this, it's handwritten but still

49
00:03:40,500 --> 00:03:45,379
 I think it can be helpful if you want to check whether you are capable of doing these computations

50
00:03:45,379 --> 00:03:47,060
 or not.

51
00:03:47,060 --> 00:03:53,139
 I made the computations for year four for the challenger here and for year two for the

52
00:03:53,139 --> 00:03:54,139
 defender.

53
00:03:54,139 --> 00:03:57,699
 So I'm quite sure that you can do it.

54
00:03:57,699 --> 00:04:03,419
 Now here we are back to what the book is saying.

55
00:04:03,419 --> 00:04:12,459
 So it's a summary and they say well we see that it's four years with an annual worth

56
00:04:12,459 --> 00:04:18,219
 of costs of minus 19,000 for the challenger and for the defender we have minus 17,000.

57
00:04:18,219 --> 00:04:23,699
 And three years so we will go for the defender.

58
00:04:23,699 --> 00:04:29,019
 We expect now, I expect to keep it for three more years but we have to perform a one year

59
00:04:29,019 --> 00:04:35,180
 later analysis and indeed if we have read the data and to see we see that some numbers

60
00:04:35,180 --> 00:04:42,899
 have changed and if we redo the analysis we see that, you see it here in the box, that

61
00:04:42,899 --> 00:04:50,019
 the numbers have indeed changed that now it seems to be that the challenger is more interesting

62
00:04:50,219 --> 00:04:54,819
 So we will replace the defender at that moment.

63
00:04:54,819 --> 00:05:02,740
 So last year so to speak we were expecting to keep the defender for three years but with

64
00:05:02,740 --> 00:05:08,899
 the analysis one year later we decided that that was not wise to keep it for another two

65
00:05:08,899 --> 00:05:19,899
 years but we would replace it by the challenger immediately.

66
00:05:20,099 --> 00:05:25,419
 Some notes, we will see an example of that later on.

67
00:05:25,419 --> 00:05:30,419
 We could do a break even analysis for instance on the market value.

68
00:05:30,419 --> 00:05:36,859
 We could say what is the market value of the defender that will make the current challenger

69
00:05:36,859 --> 00:05:41,139
 economically attractive and what is the trade in value.

70
00:05:41,139 --> 00:05:45,219
 We could do a break even analysis there.

71
00:05:45,220 --> 00:05:59,540
 Also important here is that these cost estimates are quite important because if these estimates

72
00:05:59,540 --> 00:06:02,980
 change our decision can change.

73
00:06:02,980 --> 00:06:06,180
 So that's what this is saying.

74
00:06:06,180 --> 00:06:15,980
 So that means that here the analyst and the engineer comes in, needs to be capable of

75
00:06:15,980 --> 00:06:28,579
 making an estimate as accurate as possible and not hesitate to change the estimates if necessary.

76
00:06:28,579 --> 00:06:36,379
 Now with the specified study period, we have a slightly different approach.

77
00:06:36,379 --> 00:06:38,859
 This is the example of Chicago's airport.

78
00:06:38,859 --> 00:06:41,180
 It's about the purchase of a new fire truck.

79
00:06:41,180 --> 00:06:46,860
 This fire truck is needed because an increase in firefighting capacity is needed.

80
00:06:46,860 --> 00:06:52,620
 Options are to buy an additional truck of the same capacity or to buy a new double capacity

81
00:06:52,620 --> 00:06:55,299
 truck to replace the current one.

82
00:06:55,299 --> 00:06:58,180
 Estimates are summarized in the table.

83
00:06:58,180 --> 00:07:04,540
 And the question asked is to perform a replacement analysis considering a study period of 12

84
00:07:04,540 --> 00:07:09,819
 years and considering a study period of 9 years.

85
00:07:09,819 --> 00:07:15,620
 So let's have a look.

86
00:07:15,620 --> 00:07:20,540
 Again nothing very new.

87
00:07:20,540 --> 00:07:32,420
 If we say a study period of 12 years we write down the equations for 12 years.

88
00:07:32,420 --> 00:07:35,260
 We write down the equation for the defender.

89
00:07:35,260 --> 00:07:39,980
 We write down the equation for the challenger.

90
00:07:39,980 --> 00:07:43,780
 Defender in this case is the presently owned one plus the augmentation.

91
00:07:43,780 --> 00:07:48,180
 The challenger is the double capacity truck.

92
00:07:49,019 --> 00:07:58,139
 Is there a difference between the 12 year study period and the 9 year study period?

93
00:07:58,139 --> 00:08:02,220
 Not really, it's just the number of years that you consider.

94
00:08:02,220 --> 00:08:08,660
 Then we can have another conclusion.

95
00:08:08,660 --> 00:08:17,060
 Another conclusion here we go for the double capacity truck and also here we go for the

96
00:08:17,660 --> 00:08:20,300
 double capacity truck.

97
00:08:20,300 --> 00:08:25,980
 So these computations are a little bit shorter when we have a study period given to us than

98
00:08:25,980 --> 00:08:30,379
 in case we have no study period specified.

